**Compiling a nested procedure**

int fact(int n)
{
  if (n < 1) return (1);
    else return (n * fact(n - 1));
}

assembly instruction explanation
fact:
  addi sp, sp, -8 reserves 8 bytes on stack for 2 items
  sw saves the return address x1 and argument n x10
  the body is executed as defined
    addi x5, x10, -1
    bge x5, x0, L1 //L1 is ofcourse a label defined
    addi x10, x0, 1
    addi sp, sp, 8 pops the 2 items off stack
    jalr x0, 0(x1) returns to the caller whose address is in x1
  L1:addi x10, x10, -1
     jal x1, fact calls fact and saves the caller address to x1 for later use by jalr
  add x6, x1, 0 x6 being a tempory register don't need to be written to memory
  lw x10, 0(sp)
  lw x1, 4(sp)
  addi sp, sp, 8 pop those 2 items from stack
  mul x10, x10, x6
  jalr x0, 0(x1) return to the caller whose address was saved by jal to x1 earlier